From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:45:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 032/105] logits: let the W8A16 lm_head GEMV write the
 next-token buffer directly (SGLANG_DRAFT_LOGITS_OUT=1)

_copy_logits_to_buffer widens the draft head's bf16 logits into the shared fp32
next_token_logits_buffer with a separate elementwise kernel: 14 launches / ~38 us per
W16 decode step (grid [64,1,1], 32768 hot vocab rows).

w8a16_gemv / bf16_gemv now take an optional out=, and the kernel stores
acc.to(bf16).to(out dtype) -- the bf16 round is kept even for an fp32 destination, so
the buffer ends up holding exactly what the old "bf16 result, then copy_" produced.
For a bf16 destination the extra cast folds away and the emitted code is unchanged.

Plumbing keeps the routing decision in one place: Fp8LinearMethod grows
_w8a16_gemv_ok (shared with apply) and apply_into, which returns None whenever the
GEMV path or the destination does not fit, so the caller falls back to apply.
LogitsProcessor._direct_logits_buffer offers the buffer only when every step between
the lm_head and the copy is a no-op for this batch (no logit_scale, no TP gather, no
DP scatter, no embedding bias, fp32 row-contiguous buffer no wider than vocab_size),
and _copy_logits_to_buffer short-circuits when the lm_head already wrote it.

Default off.  test/srt/layers/test_draft_logits_out.py checks the gate on CPU and
bit-identity of the fp32 out= path against the bf16 result at M in {1,2,4,16}.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
